# Floodpits Drowner: the ability's target must be "a creature with a stun counter on it", checked again as it resolves
# (CR 608.2b). Bot2 has Intruder Alarm ("Creatures don't untap during their controllers' untap steps. Whenever a creature
# enters, untap all creatures."). On turn 5 Bot1 flashes in its Drowner and stuns Bot2's tapped Llanowar Elves (the Alarm's
# untap resolves first, being on top of Bot1's trigger by APNAP order, so the counter survives: checked). On turn 7 Bot1
# activates the Drowner targeting the Elves; in response Bot2 flashes in its own Drowner, and the Alarm's untap takes a
# stun counter off the Elves instead of untapping them (CR 122.1d). The Elves no longer match, so the ability does
# nothing: Bot1's Drowner is not shuffled away and the Elves stay.

